@startuml seq-read-rates
' DF-1: Normal read — view current rates (cache-then-network, retryable)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
autonumber

actor User
participant "Rates screen" as UI
participant "RatesRepository" as Repo
database "Local cache" as Cache
participant "ApiClient" as Api
participant "Web service" as WS
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "NBP API" as NBP

User -> UI : open Rates
UI -> Repo : currentRates()
Repo -> Cache : load("rates:current")
Cache --> Repo : cached table + fetchedAt (if any)
Repo --> UI : show cached data, label "Cached · updated <time>"
Repo -> Api : GET /api/v1/rates/current (timeout 8 s)
Api -> WS : HTTPS request
WS -> DB : SELECT latest table C rows
alt latest stored table older than refresh interval
  WS -> NBP : GET /api/exchangerates/tables/C/?format=json
  NBP --> WS : table C (bid / ask)
  WS -> DB : INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
end
DB --> WS : rate rows
WS --> Api : 200 {tableNo, effectiveDate, fetchedAt, rates[]}
Api --> Repo : RateTable
Repo -> Cache : save("rates:current", data, now)
Repo --> UI : show current data, label "Live · NBP table <tableNo>"

note over Api, WS
Network error, timeout, 502/503/504:
retry up to 3 attempts (1 s, 2 s backoff ± 20 % jitter).
After the last failure the cached data stays on screen
with an "offline / could not refresh" banner.
end note
@enduml
